{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"6eff0a0b6fde23ed8994a74d6e820b7b6998daf0e100a98b684aaf64206ad6dd","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar reconciler lock subsystem (_advisory_lock, _ref_lock)","key_entities":["_advisory_lock.py:83","_ref_lock.py:194","rebar_reconciler.git_adapter","lazy_load","sys.modules","test_bridge_preview_under_sync_contention_heldout.py","commit d9e0f0e733"],"problem_keywords":["import error","module not found","standalone loader","package context","lazy loading","reconciler"],"propositions":["Commit d9e0f0e733 introduced unconditional top-level `from rebar_reconciler import git_adapter` imports at _advisory_lock.py:83 and _ref_lock.py:194, breaking standalone by-path module loading.","The bridge preview lock test fails with ModuleNotFoundError when _advisory_lock._lock_remote attempts to import rebar_reconciler, which is intentionally unavailable in standalone/installed-wheel execution contexts.","Both _advisory_lock and _ref_lock support execution by file path without package context, but the absolute imports prevent this intended execution mode.","The repair requires routing both git_adapter loads through lazy_load with the dotted key `rebar_reconciler.git_adapter` to share one canonical sys.modules object with package-context importers."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787402827427325001,"uuid":"cfbd71dd-fba9-4541-a14d-dded4006e36f"}